# =============================================================================
# miewb.env.example — template for MieWorkbench's machine-path file.
#
# Copy to <repo>/miewb.env (or, better, run scripts/setup_env.sh, which
# probes your machine and writes it for you). miewb.env is gitignored:
# it describes ONE machine, never the project.
#
# Consumers:
#   * scripts/common.py parses this file directly at import — every
#     pipeline stage, the GUI, and the tests see the same values.
#   * `source scripts/miewb_env.sh` exports these for your shell (plus
#     MIEWB_INST_DIR = the repo root), so doc examples like
#     "$MIEWB_OPTICS_PYTHON" -m pytest ... are copy-pasteable.
#   * cengine/build.sh reads MIEWB_NVCC / MIEWB_CUDA_ARCH for the CUDA
#     build.
#
# Precedence: an exported MIEWB_* environment variable beats a line
# here; a line here beats nothing (missing required keys are a hard
# error pointing back at scripts/setup_env.sh).
#
# Format rules (enforced by the parser):
#   * KEY=value, one per line; '#' lines and blanks are ignored.
#   * Values are LITERAL: no quotes, no $variable interpolation, no
#     shell syntax, no escapes. Use absolute paths.
#   * An EMPTY value (KEY=) means "this tool is deliberately not
#     installed here" — allowed for MIEWB_PVPYTHON (viz stage is then
#     skipped with a NOTICE) and the CUDA keys (CPU-only build).
# =============================================================================

# --- required external tools -------------------------------------------------
# FreeCAD 1.1.1 AppImage (runs extract_geometry / permute_model / fcserver).
MIEWB_FREECAD=/path/to/FreeCAD.AppImage

# The optics environment's python (numpy/scipy/torch-CUDA/miepython/h5py;
# runs run_trace / post_process / the engine test suite). See INSTALL.md §3.2.
MIEWB_OPTICS_PYTHON=/path/to/optics/env/bin/python

# ParaView's pvpython (viz stage renders). Leave EMPTY if this machine has
# no ParaView — the pipeline skips viz cleanly.
MIEWB_PVPYTHON=/path/to/ParaView/bin/pvpython

# --- CUDA (optional — leave both empty on CPU-only machines) -----------------
# nvcc from a CUDA >= 13 toolkit (NOT the distro /usr/bin/nvcc if it's 11.x).
MIEWB_NVCC=
# GPU SM architecture for the C engine, e.g. 89 for RTX 4090 (compute 8.9);
# setup_env.sh reads it from nvidia-smi.
MIEWB_CUDA_ARCH=

# --- optional overrides (defaults derive from the repo location) -------------
# The GUI virtualenv python (default: <repo>/env/bin/python).
# MIEWB_GUI_PYTHON=
# Geometry cache / results / optical-properties library directories
# (defaults: <repo>/geometry, <repo>/results, <repo>/opticalproperties).
# MIEWB_GEOMETRY_DIR=
# MIEWB_RESULTS_DIR=
# MIEWB_OPTPROPS_DIR=
# C-engine binary override (default: <repo>/cengine/build/miewb-trace).
# MIEWB_CENGINE=
